  "$comment": "SDK parity expectations for the 2.0.0 SDKs (v2 charter Phase 3, S4). One entry per operation in spec/v2/path-manifest.json (RFC 0172 \u00a7C.2 \u2014 the canonical unversioned operation set, vendored at CORPUS_TAG). Every entry is typed in every SDK with a mandatory symbols map: a v2 SDK has exactly one method per manifest operation (RFC 0168 \u00a7D). Checked by `node scripts/check-sdk-parity.mjs --manifest spec/v2/path-manifest.json --expectations sdk/parity-expectations-v2.json`. TypeScript symbols are `namespace.method` on OpenwopClient; Python symbols are OpenwopClient methods; Go symbols are OpenwopClient methods. Note the two SSE channels are methods too (runs.events / host.events; runs_events / host_events; StreamEvents / StreamHostEvents).",
